Zstandard (src/vendor/zstd/)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Upstream:  https://github.com/facebook/zstd
Release:   v1.5.7 (commit f8745da6ff1ad1e7bab384bd1f9d742439278e99)
License:   BSD 3-Clause. Upstream offers zstd under BSD-3-Clause or GPLv2 at
           the recipient's choice; zukomp takes and redistributes it under
           BSD-3-Clause only. The notice is reproduced verbatim in
           src/vendor/zstd/LICENSE.

  Copyright (c) Meta Platforms, Inc. and affiliates.
  Copyright (c) Yann Collet - Meta Platforms, Inc (xxHash, bundled in
                common/xxhash.h)
  Copyright (c) 2016 Tino Reichardt (common/threading.c, threading.h;
                compiled single-threaded here, so those files reduce to
                stubs)

Included: lib/zstd.h, lib/zstd_errors.h and lib/common/, lib/compress/ and
lib/decompress/, less decompress/huf_decompress_amd64.S. Not included:
dictBuilder/, legacy/, deprecated/, dll/, zdict.h and the command-line
programs. Compiled with ZSTD_DISABLE_ASM=1, ZSTD_LEGACY_SUPPORT=0 and
XXH_NAMESPACE=ZSTD_, and with its public functions' explicit default
visibility removed so that zukomp.so exports none of them.

One local patch, under tools/patches/zstd/:

  0001-drop-clang-diagnostic-pragma.patch
                                     removes a "#pragma clang diagnostic
                                     ignored" around ZSTD_defaultCMem in
                                     zstd.h. It suppresses a C++-only
                                     warning, zukomp compiles zstd as C, and
                                     R CMD check reports such pragmas. No
                                     code changes.

