LZ4 (src/vendor/lz4/)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Upstream:  https://github.com/lz4/lz4
Release:   v1.10.0 (commit ebb370ca83af193212df4dcbadcc5d87bc0de2f0)
License:   BSD 2-Clause, the licence of the LZ4 library (lib/); the GPLv2
           that covers lz4's command-line programs does not apply, as no
           program is included. The notice is reproduced verbatim in
           src/vendor/lz4/LICENSE.

  Copyright (C) 2011-2023, Yann Collet.

Included: lz4.c, lz4.h, lz4frame.c, lz4frame.h, lz4hc.c, lz4hc.h, xxhash.c
and xxhash.h from lib/. Not included: lz4file.c, lz4frame_static.h, the dll
files and the programs. Compiled with XXH_NAMESPACE=LZ4_ and NDEBUG, and
with its public functions' explicit default visibility removed so that
zukomp.so exports none of them.

One local patch, under tools/patches/lz4/:

  0001-drop-unused-function-pragmas.patch
                                     removes two "#pragma ... diagnostic
                                     ignored -Wunused-function" lines from
                                     lz4hc.c, which R CMD check reports. No
                                     code changes.

Yann Collet, Meta Platforms, Inc. and affiliates, and Tino Reichardt are
listed in Authors@R in DESCRIPTION, with 'cph' roles and, for the two people,
'ctb'. LICENSE.note at the top of the source package summarises all three
bundled licences.

No other modification is made to the zstd or lz4 sources. Unlike miniz,
neither library's headers are installed and neither is part of
libzukomp.a: both exist only compiled into <zukomp>/libs/, and their
licences are installed as <zukomp>/licenses/zstd-LICENSE and
<zukomp>/licenses/lz4-LICENSE.
